This year’s SIGCSE Technical Symposium includes two invited keynote speakers. Dr. Cecilia Aragon is a Professor and Director of the Human-Centered Data Science Lab at the University of Washington. She will speak at the opening plenary session about human-centered artificial intelligence and its future directions. Jamika D. Burge, Ph.D. is the CEO and Co-Founder of blackcomputeHER.org, INC. She will speak about intersectionality in computing and discuss how its alignment to CS education can meet the needs of all students.
Our Friday plenary session will include the presentation of three SIGCSE awards. Dr. Manuel PérezQuiñones is the recipient of the 2025 ACM SIGCSE Award for Distinguished Service to the Computer Science Education Community. Dr. Mitch Resnick is the 2025 SIGCSE Award for Outstanding


