Contribution to Computer Science Education. Dr. Jonathan Mwaura is the recipient of the 2025 SIGCSE Broadening Participation in Computing Education Award. The presentation of these awards will be followed by a short panel session focused on the future of computer science education. The panel will consist of the three award winners and will be moderated by Dan Garcia, Secretary of the SIGCSE Board. Congratulations to all of the award winners!
We would also like to express our sincere gratitude to the exhibitors and supporters that are contributing to this year’s SIGCSE Technical Symposium. It would not be possible to put on the Technical Symposium without their valued support. The 2025 supporters include:
● Platinum: NSF, Google, and GitHub Education ● Gold: Rephactor, Codio, and MongoDB ● Silver: Vocareum, ABET ● Bronze: PrairieLearn
The 2025 SIGCSE Technical Symposium is successful thanks to the contributions of many individuals and organizations. We would like to sincerely thank the ACM staff, the Site Selection Committee, the SIGCSE Board, and the SIGCSE Technical Symposium Steering Committee for all of their hard work and guidance. Other contributors who we would like to thank include Accent, Whova, Sheridan, WRG Design, the David L. Lawrence Convention Center, Visit Pittsburgh, conf.researchr.org, and EasyChair. We would especially like to thank the incredible team at DLPlan for all of their work. Thanks as well to all of our student volunteers, committee members, reviewers, and others who contributed to the success of this year’s Technical Symposium - we could not have done it without you!
Thank you to our attendees for joining us in Pittsburgh, either in-person or virtually, and thank you to all of you who contributed your work to this years’ program. We truly hope that the 2025 SIGCSE Technical Symposium is a constructive, informative, and meaningful experience that will benefit you and your students.
